[ti:Never Too Old To Learn]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.57]How long has Mr. Page been teaching? | 佩奇先生任教多久了？
[00:14.97]I have just received a letter from my old school, informing me that my former headmaster, Mr. Stuart Page, will be retiring next week. | 我刚收到母校的一封信，通知我以前的老校长斯图尔特·佩奇先生下星期就要退休了。
[00:27.95]Pupils of the school old and new, will be sending him a present to mark the occasion. | 新老学生将为纪念这一日子给他送一件礼物。
[00:35.53]All those who have contributed towards the gift will sign their names in a large album which will be sent to the headmaster's home. | 所有凑钱买此礼品的人都将把自己的名字签在一本大签名簿上，签名簿将被送到老校长家中。
[00:45.53]We shall all remember Mr. Page for his patience and understanding and for the kindly encouragement he gave us when we went so unwillingly to school. | 我们不会忘记佩奇先生的耐心和理解，不会忘记我们极不愿意上学时他给予我们的亲切鼓励。
[00:59.48]A great many former pupils will be attending a farewell dinner in his honour next Thursday. | 下星期四，许多他昔日的学生将参加为他举行的告别宴会。
[01:07.40]It is a curious coincidence that the day before his retirement, Mr. Page will have been teaching for a total of forty years. | 佩奇先生退休的前一天正好是他执教整40年的日子，真是奇妙的巧合。
[01:18.66]After he has retired he will devote himself to gardening. | 退休后，他将致力于园艺。
[01:24.22]For him, this will be an entirely new hobby. | 对他来说，这将是一种全新的爱好。
[01:29.06]But this does not matter, for, as he has often remarked, one is never too old to learn. | 这没有关系，因为正如他常说的那样，活到老学到老。
